   "id": 532720,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the surface area of the equilateral triangular prism shown.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5b1df1c1aad02af9.png\" alt=\"An equilateral triangular prism. The sides of the triangle measure 10 centimeters. The height of the triangle measures 8.66 centimeters. The length of the prism measures 10 centimeters.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The surface area of a right prism where <i>B</i> is the area of the base, <i>p</i> is the perimeter of the base, and <i>h</i> is the height is <span data-math=\"SA = 2B + ph\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The area of the triangular base is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}bh\"></span>, where <i>b</i> represents the base and <i>h</i> represents the height.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}bh = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {{\\text{10 cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{8}}{\\text{.66 cm}}} \\right) = {\\text{ 43}}{\\text{.3 c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The perimeter of the base <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  }}p{\\text{  =  10 cm  +  10 cm  +  10 cm  =  30 cm}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\" = {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {43.3{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {30{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {10{\\text{ cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}86.6{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} + {\\text{ }}300{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} = {\\text{ }}386.6{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area is 386.6 square centimeters.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"386.6\\,\\text{cm}{^2}\">386.6\\,\\text{cm}{^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
